WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.912
The Users Registration feature lets visitors create their own accounts on an Orchard Core site.

00:00:06.912 --> 00:00:11.829
In this video, you enable it, follow three visitors through the Register page,

00:00:11.829 --> 00:00:16.980
check their accounts by email and by approval, and see how login providers fit in.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:28.219
Without the Users Registration feature, only administrators create accounts, one by one, in the Users list.

00:00:28.219 --> 00:00:32.860
The login page has no link for visitors who want an account of their own.

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:37.869
The feature adds a Register page, and a link to it on the login page.

00:00:37.869 --> 00:00:39.856
It also adds a settings page.

00:00:39.856 --> 00:00:44.115
Its options decide how each account is checked before it can be used,

00:00:44.115 --> 00:00:46.670
and which theme the Register page uses.

00:00:50.909 --> 00:00:55.491
Registration is a feature, so it stays off until you enable it.

00:00:55.491 --> 00:00:59.409
Under Tools, Features, search for Users Registration.

00:00:59.876 --> 00:01:01.016
Select Enable.

00:01:01.016 --> 00:01:05.349
A message confirms that the feature was enabled, and its row lists the

00:01:05.349 --> 00:01:07.002
features it depends on:

00:01:07.002 --> 00:01:08.256
Users and Email.

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:15.259
Email matters here, because confirmation messages leave through the Default provider chosen under

00:01:15.259 --> 00:01:19.964
Settings, Communication, Email, and without a provider no message is sent.

00:01:19.964 --> 00:01:23.962
This site uses an SMTP provider that delivers to a test inbox.

00:01:28.231 --> 00:01:31.904
The options live under Settings, Security, Registration.

00:01:31.904 --> 00:01:35.874
The page has three checkboxes, and all of them start cleared.

00:01:35.874 --> 00:01:40.141
Two decide how an account is checked, and the third sets the theme

00:01:40.141 --> 00:01:41.741
of the Register page.

00:01:42.267 --> 00:01:47.237
The first checkbox, Users must verify their email address, sends each visitor a

00:01:47.237 --> 00:01:48.758
message with a link.

00:01:48.758 --> 00:01:53.319
Selecting it shows a warning that users whose email address has not been

00:01:53.319 --> 00:01:56.477
confirmed cannot log in or reset their password.

00:01:56.935 --> 00:02:01.681
The second checkbox, Users must be approved before they can log in, creates

00:02:01.681 --> 00:02:06.075
every registered account disabled, until an administrator enables it.

00:02:06.543 --> 00:02:11.256
The third checkbox, Use site theme for registration page, shows the Register page

00:02:11.256 --> 00:02:14.560
in the design of your site, instead of the admin theme.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.673
It requires an active site theme.

00:02:20.888 --> 00:02:24.193
A visitor who is not signed in opens the login page.

00:02:24.193 --> 00:02:27.898
Under the Log in button is the link Register as a new user,

00:02:27.898 --> 00:02:30.178
which opens the registration form.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:35.372
The form, headed Register a new account, asks for a username, an email

00:02:35.372 --> 00:02:38.741
address, and a password, which is entered twice.

00:02:38.741 --> 00:02:41.860
Let's fill it in for a visitor called Jamie.

00:02:42.323 --> 00:02:44.911
Selecting Register creates the account.

00:02:44.911 --> 00:02:49.455
Because no option is selected, the account works at once, and the visitor

00:02:49.455 --> 00:02:52.043
is signed in and sent to the home page.

00:02:56.262 --> 00:03:01.927
On the Registration settings page, select Users must verify their email address, and save.

00:03:01.927 --> 00:03:06.412
The site confirms with the message Site settings updated successfully.

00:03:08.035 --> 00:03:11.970
A second visitor, Morgan, registers with the same form.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:18.355
This time, Register opens the page Email confirmation sent, and the visitor is not signed in.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:22.483
The message Confirm your account is waiting in the test inbox.

00:03:22.483 --> 00:03:26.480
It greets the visitor by username, and holds a link that stays valid

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:27.830
for a limited time.

00:03:28.297 --> 00:03:33.920
Following the link opens the Email confirmation page, which thanks the visitor for confirming.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:36.337
From then on, the visitor can log in.

00:03:40.539 --> 00:03:45.391
To review each registration yourself, clear the email option on the same page,

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:48.164
so that this example shows approval alone.

00:03:48.164 --> 00:03:52.439
Then select Users must be approved before they can log in, and save.

00:03:54.091 --> 00:03:56.393
A third visitor, Riley, registers.

00:03:56.393 --> 00:04:00.710
The account is created disabled, so the visitor is not signed in, and

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:05.661
the User Registration Pending page explains that the account has to be approved.

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:12.689
Under Access Control, Users, the list shows Riley's account with a Disabled badge.

00:04:12.689 --> 00:04:15.596
Open its Actions menu, and select Enable.

00:04:16.048 --> 00:04:17.240
Confirm with Ok.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:22.006
The message User account was successfully enabled appears, and the visitor can log

00:04:22.006 --> 00:04:23.198
in from then on.

00:04:27.398 --> 00:04:30.823
Visitors can also register with a login provider.

00:04:30.823 --> 00:04:37.610
Enabling Google Authentication, GitHub Authentication or Meta Login adds an External Authentication tab

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:41.658
to the Registration settings page, next to the General tab.

00:04:42.408 --> 00:04:47.495
Among its options are Disable new external registration, Do not ask username, Do

00:04:47.495 --> 00:04:51.163
not ask email address, and Do not create local password.

00:04:51.163 --> 00:04:56.664
Selecting the username, email and password options together lets the account be created

00:04:56.664 --> 00:04:59.208
without showing the visitor any form.

00:04:59.958 --> 00:05:05.920
Accounts created through a provider follow the same email and approval options as the Register page.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:11.376
Each provider also needs credentials from its own developer portal, which the documentation

00:05:11.376 --> 00:05:13.738
of Google, GitHub and Meta explains.

00:05:15.738 --> 00:05:21.223
Users Registration gives visitors a Register page, and with an email provider configured,

00:05:21.223 --> 00:05:25.207
its options let you check each account by email or by approval.

00:05:25.207 --> 00:05:26.708
Thanks for watching.

